    "result": "Perfect! All tests are passing and all public exports remain intact. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Summary\n\nI fixed two failing tests in the frai-core test suite:\n\n### 1. **Governance test failure** - Missing named export\n**File:** `src/finetune/index.js`\n- **Issue:** The test was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only exported as part of the default export.\n- **Fix:** Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` from schema.js, while keeping them in the default export for backward compatibility.\n\n### 2. **Eval test failure** - Wrong parameter usage\n**File:** `src/eval/metrics.js`\n- **Issue:** The `toxicityMetric` function was receiving `references` as its second parameter (from `runEvaluations`), which was being used as the `bannedTerms` list. This caused reference text to be incorrectly flagged as toxic.\n- **Fix:** Changed the function signature to accept `references` as a parameter (for API consistency) but always use `defaultBannedTerms` internally, ignoring the references parameter.\n\nAll 28 tests now pass, and every existing public export continues to work.",
